  /* Above ~760px there's room to put the photos and the buy panel side by
     side instead of stacking them — on a laptop screen the old stacked
     layout meant scrolling past a full-width image before any of the
     color/size/price/CTA info came into view, so nothing about a product
     was visible in one screen at once. Row layout fixes that: the whole
     card (photo + every control + the Buy button) fits in view together
     on typical desktop heights. Below 760px there usually isn't enough
     width left for the info column to stay readable once the photo takes
     its share, so it stays stacked (the original, still-correct
